       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the usual maximum adult dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose there is a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Amlodipine's long half-life (30\u201350 hours) would make the effects last.\n\nPlease check whether one of these was intended:\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, the usual starting dose.\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose.\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, which is sometimes used in frail or elderly patients, or with hepatic impairment.\n\nIf 50 mg is correct, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though it would probably also need pharmacist or prescriber verification. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
