       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. No indication supports 50 mg of amlodipine daily. It is five times the labeled maximum, and I think it could seriously harm the patient. You also haven't given a clinical rationale.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **If the dose is a mistake**, give me the intended dose, such as 5 mg or 10 mg once daily, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **If you have a real reason for the higher dose**, such as a specialist recommendation, please discuss it with the pharmacist and the attending. The order can then go through your hospital's high-dose override process.\n- **If the patient needs more blood pressure control than 10 mg gives**, adding a second agent from a different class is the usual approach. I can enter that order if you tell me which drug."
